version: 0_3_3
status: PC-controlled on-demand ESP camera session candidate
previous_version: 0_3_2
passed_baseline: 0_2_4
notes: The owner explicitly requested the next patch after V032. V033 changes ESP camera transport so connecting to an ESP does not start image transfer. PC Studio first connects to the ESP status/control surface, then Start Stream sends the complete validated OV2640 runtime camera settings to the ESP, activates the ESP camera session, and only then starts bounded PC-side /capture polling. Stop Stream ends polling and disables ESP image responses while keeping the device connected. The ESP therefore sends image bytes only in response to an active PC-started session and image request. V032 legacy raw device upload and simulation remain compatible. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road traffic control remains disabled.
